# Development-stage project policy

Follow the repository-root `AGENTS.md` development-stage and scope/safety policy.
AI Cockpit / Jarvis is in active development: existing application data is
disposable. Prioritize a current, correct, coherent long-term implementation over
backward compatibility or preserving old development data. Update all consumers
and tests together, and remove unnecessary legacy compatibility code.

Necessary local migrations and precisely scoped development-data resets are
normal implementation work; data preservation alone is not an approval blocker.
Preserve source/uncommitted work, credentials and unrelated files, confirm exact
reset targets and writer shutdown, and retain security/durability guarantees.
Do not infer authorization for production enablement or external account/device
changes. Reassess this policy explicitly before production rollout.
